  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Support Flood Affected Vulunerable Households in Koch and Rubkona Counties in Unity State, South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of sanitary kits for women of reproductive age and adolescent girls in Koch and Rubkona, (5) Provision of emergency health services through mobile clinics to the affected populations and Screening of Older persons and Persons with Disability, children under 5 years old and Pregnant and lactating mothers and provision of supplementary feeding to malnourished children under 5 years old</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of treated mosquito nets, WASH  kits including jerrycans, Soaps, Aqua tabs, PUR, chlorine for water treatment and purification</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strenghtening community engagment, awareness and sensitization activities on hygiene promotion education to reduce outbreak of diseases e.g. cholera and COVID-19 Since people are congested in open space</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening community engagement through awareness, education, preparedness, and prediction and warning systems using older persons as resourceful persons in community to reduce the disruptive impacts of floodings on community.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting the communities through the provision of mosquito nets, plastic sheets and floor mats  to protect against malaria</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will target women (especailly Pregnant women and lactating mothers), children (girls and boys), older people and persons with disabilities and their households to ensure that the specific needs of flood affected persons  are met.</narrative>
  </description>
